    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d808">

                <pb facs="1172" n="1040" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg1040"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.05/84: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-04T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 4,
                                1927—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 4—10:17
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>5. American consul general at Shanghai reported January 3d that rendition of
                    Mixed Court was effected by exchange of notes dated December 31st<anchor n="31a"
                        xml:id="d808-f1"/> and that first session of Provisional Court would be held
                    January 4th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d808-f1" n="31a" xml:id="d808-f1-content">
                <p>For the English text of the exchange of notes on Dec. 31, 1926, see The Municipal
                    Gazette (official organ of the Council for the Foreign Settlement of Shanghai),
                    vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">xx</hi>, No. 1064 (Feb. 18, 1927), p. 47; cf.
                    The China Year Book, 1928, p. 468.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
